"texte": [
"Over the course of the last decade, the massive rise of digital technologies has profoundly modified the structure of our daily life.",
"In the past, the boundaries between professional space and the private sphere were clearly delimited by standard office hours.",
"People used to leave their workplace at five PM, leaving professional files behind until the following morning.",
"Today, this indispensable separation has blurred to the point of becoming almost completely invisible for a majority of workers.",
"The widespread development of remote work offers undeniable flexibility, but it also hides subtle psychological traps.",
"Many employees confess that they now experience great difficulty interrupting their work in the evening at home.",
"They consult their digital messages at inappropriate hours and feel an implicit obligation to remain connected permanently to the company.",
"This hyperconnectivity engenders a new type of cognitive fatigue, frequently termed by experts as digital mental load.",
"Parallelly, our modern consumption habits have followed a very similar trajectory centered on absolute immediacy.",
"The fact that one can purchase any product in a single click has developed a form of chronic impatience within consumers.",
"Face to this constant acceleration, citizen movements emerge to advocate for a healthy return to voluntary slowness.",
"Learning how to set clear technological boundaries has become indispensable if one wishes to preserve one's psychological balance."
],
